@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Gemini wire-response validation classes
hide empty members
' @class backend.gemini.GenerateResponse
class GenerateResponse {
  model_validate_json(content) {inherited}
}
' @class backend.gemini.Candidate
class Candidate {
  finishReason: str | None
}
' @class backend.gemini.Content
class Content {
  role: str | None
}
' @class backend.gemini.Part
class Part {
  text: str | None
  thought: bool = false
}
' @class backend.gemini.PromptFeedback
class PromptFeedback {
  blockReason: str | None
}
GenerateResponse "0..*" --> "0..*" Candidate : candidates
GenerateResponse "0..*" --> "0..1" PromptFeedback : promptFeedback
Candidate "0..*" --> "0..1" Content : content
Content "0..*" --> "0..*" Part : parts
note bottom of Candidate
  Service selects the first candidate.
  STOP is required; truncation, blocking,
  absent content and invalid JSON fail explicitly.
end note
note bottom of Part
  Only nonempty text from non-thought parts
  contributes to the public result.
end note
legend bottom
  All five primary classes live in backend.gemini and extend BaseModel.
  Optional fields/list defaults justify 0..1 and 0..*.
  They validate upstream wire data, not stored corpus entities.
  These classes are distinct from public TranslationContent/ChatResponse DTOs.
endlegend
@enduml
